  "term": "Paxil",
  "definition": "Paxil is the hydrochloride salt form of paroxetine, a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor with antidepressant and anxiety-reducing effects. It works by blocking the presynaptic reuptake of serotonin, increasing serotonin activity in the synapse and helping relieve symptoms of depression.",
